// =====================================================================
// Seed Company — date dimension with fiscal year columns
//
// Extends the shared `dim_dates` rather than copying it, so the base
// calendar (one row per day, 2013 to today) stays owned by
// `01 demo ecommerce/` and is not modified here.
//
// Seed Company's fiscal year runs 1 Oct to 30 Sep, named by the ENDING
// calendar year: 2026 = 1 Oct 2025 -> 30 Sep 2026.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Built on `year` / `month_number`, NOT on date arithmetic
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// The obvious derivation counts months from an anchor Oct 1 with
// date_diff. It is off by a whole month. `date_key` is a DATE, and
// Holistics casts it to timestamptz then applies the tenant timezone
// (America/Los_Angeles here), which rolls every month-start back into
// the previous month, while the anchor literal carries its own offset
// and does not shift. Verified: it produced fiscal years running
// 1 Nov to 31 Oct.
//
// `year` and `month_number` come from `to_char()` evaluated in the
// warehouse on the raw date, so they carry no timezone distortion.
// Reading them is both simpler and correct. This also keeps the whole
// thing warehouse-agnostic, which matters while Seed's warehouse is
// still unconfirmed (Snowflake per Lori, Redshift per Chukwudi).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Current fiscal year, with no date written down
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// The base `dim_dates` query is `generate_series(... , current_date, ...)`,
// so the last row in the calendar is always today. That makes
// `max(fiscal_year)` the fiscal year containing today, by construction.
// `fiscal_year_offset` is 0 for the current fiscal year and -1 for the
// prior one, and rolls over on 1 October with nothing to edit.
//
// This is why there is no @now anywhere in this file. @now inlines as a
// full timestamp, so the generated SQL changes on every execution and
// the query cache never hits — bad for a cost-sensitive customer.
// =====================================================================
Model seed_dim_dates = dim_dates.extend({
  label: 'Seed Dim Dates'
  description: 'Shared date dimension plus Seed Company fiscal year columns (FY runs Oct 1 - Sep 30, named by ending year).'

  dimension fiscal_year {
    label: 'Fiscal Year'
    type: 'number'
    description: 'Fiscal year number, named by the ending calendar year. Oct 2025 - Sep 2026 = 2026.'
    definition: @aql case(
        when: cast(seed_dim_dates.month_number, 'number') >= 10
        , then: cast(seed_dim_dates.year, 'number') + 1
        , else: cast(seed_dim_dates.year, 'number')
      ) ;;
  }

  dimension fiscal_year_label {
    label: 'Fiscal Year Label'
    type: 'text'
    description: "Display form of the fiscal year, e.g. 'FY26'."
    definition: @aql concat('FY', cast(seed_dim_dates.fiscal_year - 2000, 'text')) ;;
  }

  dimension fiscal_quarter {
    label: 'Fiscal Quarter'
    type: 'text'
    description: 'Fiscal quarter. Q1 = Oct-Dec, Q2 = Jan-Mar, Q3 = Apr-Jun, Q4 = Jul-Sep.'
    definition: @aql case(
        when: cast(seed_dim_dates.month_number, 'number') >= 10, then: 'Q1'
        , when: cast(seed_dim_dates.month_number, 'number') >= 7, then: 'Q4'
        , when: cast(seed_dim_dates.month_number, 'number') >= 4, then: 'Q3'
        , else: 'Q2'
      ) ;;
  }

  dimension fiscal_year_offset {
    label: 'Fiscal Year Offset'
    type: 'number'
    description: '0 = current fiscal year, -1 = prior fiscal year. Resolves against today, never needs editing.'
    definition: @aql seed_dim_dates.fiscal_year - max(seed_dim_dates.fiscal_year) ;;
  }
})
